From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: The large-screen layout drawn at 1280x640, the panel's size

At 1x the core drew the large-screen layout (001) into a 1920x960 buffer,
for RetroArch to scale down to 1280x640 on the RG52 Mini's panel: 2.25 times
the pixels, 2.45 ms of the GPU's time a frame in Super Mario 3D Land. At
8/3 instead of 4 the buffer is 1280x640, 1.21 ms, and the picture is the
same size (the top screen 1066x640, the bottom one 213x160).

--- a/src/citra_libretro/emu_window/libretro_window.cpp
+++ b/src/citra_libretro/emu_window/libretro_window.cpp
@@ -267,8 +267,12 @@
         if (scaling < 4) {
             // Unfortunately, to get this aspect ratio correct (and have non-blurry 1x scaling),
             //  we have to have a pretty large buffer for the minimum ratio.
-            baseX *= 4;
-            baseY *= 4;
+            // dArkOS: 8/3 instead of 4, 1280x640, the size the RG52 Mini's 1280x720 panel
+            // shows it at. At 1920x960 the core's present pass drew 2.25 times the pixels for
+            // RetroArch to scale back down: 2.45 ms of the Mali-G52's time a frame in Super
+            // Mario 3D Land, 1.21 ms at 1280x640.
+            baseX = baseX * 8 / 3;
+            baseY = baseY * 8 / 3;
         } else {
             baseX *= scaling;
             baseY *= scaling;
